[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah.

564
00:52:58,975 --> 00:53:09,103
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I think it's, like, the sutta is not so much, like, trying to give you, like, the perfect answer, but actually encourage to contemplate, if you are still suffering, it's because you fall into one of these four categories.

565
00:53:09,163 --> 00:53:09,383
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah,

566
00:53:12,780 --> 00:53:21,388
[SPEAKER_04]: When anything happens to you, on account of anybody, it's because, fundamentally, you still, to some extent, assume that the suffering arose because of them.

567
00:53:21,629 --> 00:53:21,849
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

568
00:53:23,010 --> 00:53:31,338
[SPEAKER_04]: When you feel helpless and frustrated and angry with yourself, it's because you think that you created your suffering.

569
00:53:32,238 --> 00:53:37,924
[SPEAKER_04]: When you feel helpless as well, it's also because you think that it's randomly arisen.

570
00:53:40,876 --> 00:53:55,321
