00:53:57,302 --> 00:53:58,442
[SPEAKER_04]: All completely overlooking.

572
00:53:58,582 --> 00:53:58,762
[SPEAKER_04]: No.

573
00:53:59,142 --> 00:54:06,685
[SPEAKER_04]: It's like if there is no ignorance and the Pāṭṭhī-jīsā-mupādā thing says suffering cannot arise.

574
00:54:08,907 --> 00:54:19,375
[SPEAKER_04]: Even if you wanted to arise, even if other people do bad things to you, even if random events happen, suffering can arise, if you don't have ignorance of parinirvāpa.

575
00:54:22,317 --> 00:54:26,220
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, another point I wanted to mention also.

576
00:54:26,920 --> 00:54:31,484
