577
00:54:32,725 --> 00:54:35,847
[SPEAKER_00]: And I think it's... how do you say?

578
00:54:40,247 --> 00:54:41,547
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, that's a good point.

579
00:54:41,567 --> 00:54:44,688
[SPEAKER_00]: Because willpower, as we just said, even scientists recognize willpower is not limitless.

580
00:55:07,384 --> 00:55:23,993
[SPEAKER_04]: So, that brings it back to the whole point that we mentioned, that it's all of the wholesome qualities, and the unwholesome ones as well, they have their root in the mind, in the citta, not in what you intentionally do in this moment.

581
00:55:24,933 --> 00:55:36,279
[SPEAKER_04]: So, it's what you have been inclining the mind towards, that becomes all of the awakening factors, all of the faculties, all of the

582
00:55:37,001 --> 00:55:45,947
[SPEAKER_04]: The things that basically... and that's why noble disciples, for example, it's like they cannot do certain things.

583
00:55:46,167 --> 00:55:50,550
[SPEAKER_04]: They cannot completely forget the dhamma.

584
00:55:50,570 --> 00:55:51,731
[SPEAKER_04]: They cannot kill.

585
00:55:51,771 --> 00:55:54,833
[SPEAKER_04]: They can't kill an arahant, kill the mother, kill the father.

586
00:55:55,613 --> 00:56:03,839
[SPEAKER_04]: They cannot lose their context, the perspective that they have developed, because it's not about them, kind of.

587
00:56:05,216 --> 00:56:29,281
[SPEAKER_04]: Being so on the ball and perfectly attentive all the time, it's about just the mind having been established, like a certain basis, certain framework that you built up, and then, regardless of what you do, nothing can take that away, because it's become fully ingrained and settled in.

588
00:56:30,081 --> 00:56:33,042
[SPEAKER_04]: So, like, same, anāgāmī, free from sensuality.

589
00:56:34,000 --> 00:56:40,362
[SPEAKER_04]: It's not because he's constantly thinking about, oh, this is dangerous, this is dangerous, I shouldn't engage with this.

590
00:56:40,482 --> 00:56:41,322
[SPEAKER_04]: Well, that's not freedom.

591
00:56:42,602 --> 00:57:00,247
[SPEAKER_04]: It's like, even if you completely relax and throw your hands up in the air, and just kick your legs up and drink tea or whatever, and just don't think about the dhamma ever, the mind doesn't have those inclinations, because it's been developed beforehand in that way.

592
00:57:01,045 --> 00:57:17,093
[SPEAKER_04]: So, then you realize limitless effort, or limitless energy, to not engage in these things, because the place from which the pressure actually came from, the mind, has no interest in those things anymore.

593
00:57:17,133 --> 00:57:19,494
[SPEAKER_04]: So, the effort is basically effortless.

594
00:57:19,554 --> 00:57:27,738
[SPEAKER_04]: It's like, I don't need to keep telling it, like, oh, don't do that, don't do that, like I did, like I did before.

